Widdershins is a poorer neighborhood in the southern part of [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]]. Hugging the north bank of the Fousan River, Widdershins is where many of the members of the service industry in the city live, as they cannot afford the rent required to live near their place of work. Widdershins is nearly as poor as [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/index|Sableclutch]], and holds the factories that still run in the city. The [[Org/Threshold Authority/index|Threshold Authority]] keeps the district, as it does Sableclutch. The name is the old word for counterclockwise, against the sun, and every mollusk on [[Færrin]] has a shell that coils that way. A manhole at the far end of a small open-air market drops into the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sewers|sewers]], where a pumping floor leads into the tunnels the [[Anti-Zorbon Taskforce|Anti-Zorbon Taskforce]] used.

Anchor Boulevard is one of the larger streets through the district, carrying traffic rather than stopping it. At 412 sits a [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/Gas-n-Go|Gas-n-Go]] auto body shop.
